## NOTE — PARKED, NOT CLAIMABLE

**HELD until §5.1 (the semantic-independence proof) is approved** — operator decision
2026-06-27. This bundles the three parked WCI follow-ons (WCI-4 label+payoff, §5.1 proof
contract, WCI-6 auto-slice) that the MVP explicitly EXCLUDES.

TYPE: **droid-build** (gated). It is a true successor of the WCI-MVP ticket (`depends_on: WCI`).

Why grouped / held: per `DSGN-WCI-reshape.md` §5.1, §7.1 (F1), §7.3 — concurrency from a
`merge_after` label is only safe behind a positive semantic-independence certificate. The
operator chose to land the label AND its concurrency payoff together with §5.1, so none of them
ship in the WCI-1+WCI-2 MVP. The F1 invariant is already proven; what is missing is the §5.1
proof contract itself, which is produced + adversarially reviewed by the **`DSGN-WCI-PROOF`**
ticket (a design/proof pass, ACTIVE now, parallel to WCI-MVP) before this builds.

**This ticket needs BOTH prerequisites** (see the `real-dep:` marker above): the board
`depends_on: WCI` carries the **build-dep** (WCI-MVP must land on master — it extends the MVP's
reconcile/ordering layer), and `DSGN-WCI-PROOF` carries the **sign-off gate** (the §5.1
semantic-independence proof must be operator-approved). `depends_on:` lists only `WCI` because
`DSGN-WCI-PROOF` is a design/approval gate, not a board build done-marker; the `real-dep:`
marker + this paragraph make the second prerequisite visible to the WCI-enforcer and to a human.
NOTHING here un-parks until WCI-MVP is landed AND DSGN-WCI-PROOF is approved.

Un-park / activation checklist:
1. WCI-MVP (WCI-1 + WCI-2) landed on master.  [BUILD-DEP — board `depends_on: WCI`]
2. `DSGN-WCI-PROOF` approved: §5.1 semantic-independence proof contract specified AND
   adversarially reviewed/operator-approved.  [SIGN-OFF — `real-dep:` marker above]
3. Operator sign-off to lift the hold; `owns:` + build prompt defined.
4. ADR-0008 Phase-2 conflict-rate tripwire honored for the WCI-6 auto-slice half.
